/**
 * Databricks as taught in two Packt courses on Coursera, transcripts pulled 2026-11-05:
 *  - "Fundamentals of Azure Databricks" (the "Mastering Azure Databricks for Data Engineers" videos): the five modules
 *    with spoken text cover data engineering, Apache Spark, the platform, the workspace, clusters, notebooks and DBFS.
 *    The later topics of its syllabus (Unity Catalog, Delta Lake, Autoloader, Delta Live Tables, Repos, Workflows,
 *    REST API and CLI, the capstone) appear here only with what the "About the Course" and platform lectures say.
 *  - "Databricks Certified Associate Developer for Apache Spark using Python": only the section overviews were pulled,
 *    so its cards carry the syllabus, not demos.
 * Every definition, use case, command and figure comes from those transcripts and nothing else; `facts[].at` names the
 * lesson. The automatic transcription writes "data breaks", "Apache's Park", "debut" (DBU) and "Hadlow"; the cards use
 * the real names. A third transcript, "Data Management with Databricks: Big Data with Delta Lakes", arrived empty.
 */
